  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Two-Headed Boy (Neutral Milk Hotel cover)** (1 review): The band covered the Neutral Milk Hotel track, though the singer missed some lyrics [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Somebody Else's Parking Lot in Santa Cruz (The Extra Glenns)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **West Country Dream**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Maize Stalk Drinking Blood**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **No, I Can't**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Standard Bitter Love Song #1**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Doctor Wu (Steely Dan cover)**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **You're in Maya**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **Jam Eater Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg1999-10-09.aud.192mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 13 songs; 37 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The recording is described as simultaneously the best and worst the reviewer has heard [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Going to Georgia, Prana Ferox, and Standard Bitter Love Song played better than ever [2]",
